scibar Changes
==============


Current WIP
------------
- NEW: support setting background color in zero friction API exportColorbar via new field in ExportOpts
- NEW: add TGA export option in raster pathway
- NEW: add example with superscript, thanks to inter font capabilities
- DOC: clarify UTF-8, math, superscript etc capabilities/support in FAQ
- NEW: add zero_friction_high_res example demonstrating high-resolution output
  from the zero-friction API (set only the long side of the canvas, or both,
  in ExportOpts) for both PNG and SVG
- FIX: reserve space at the horizontal ends of the colorbar for the outer tick
  labels, so scaled-up fonts no longer clip the first/last label at the canvas
  edge (font-size-anchored; applies to raster and SVG identically)
- FIX: add font-anchored breathing room above and below vertical colorbars, so
  the title label and the bottom tick label's descenders no longer crowd the
  canvas edge at larger font sizes


Version 0.2.0 -- Pixel perfect alignment and custom fonts for SVG
-------------------------------------------------------------------
- FIX: fix tick/colorbar border anti-aliasing mismatch in raster output
- FIX: fix collision between colorbar label text and top-most tick label text in vertical layout (raster + vector)
- CHG: center tick label text vertically on ticks, instead of previous behaviour that had the font baseline on the tick
- CHG: Full consistency over different SVG rendering backends (rsvglib vs. chrome/firefix/inkscape) by not relying on dominant-baseline attribute, which is still missing support in rsvglib-based software
- NEW: add new example tick_diagnostic
- NEW: support custom fonts in SVG pipeline, both referenced (font-family can be auto-computed from embedded or custom font TTF file, or manually specified) and embedded (embedded font support depends on viewer though). This way, we offer everything we can with regards to making the raster and vector versions look as similar as possible.


